# Copy to .env and fill in. Read by config.Load() AND by the Makefile.
# The value below matches the Postgres 18 of docker-compose.yml (port 5433).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://flowlio:flowlio@localhost:5433/flowlio?sslmode=disable
ADDR=:8080
ENV=dev
MODE=local

# MODE decides the bootstrap: `local` (no account, this process issues its own admin token on the
# first start and writes it to a 0600 file) or `hosted` (operated deployment, bootstrap disabled,
# the admin token comes from the environment).
#
# ADMIN_TOKEN belongs to hosted mode and to it alone. Missing there, the instance would answer 401
# to its own operator with no way back in. SET HERE, IN LOCAL MODE, THE PROCESS REFUSES TO START:
# local mode issues its own token and would ignore this one, leaving a live administration secret
# in an environment where you believe it is in use. Mint one with:
#   go run ./cmd/api mint-admin-token
# ADMIN_TOKEN=

# Browser origins allowed to call the API, comma-separated.
#
# Default when absent: https://flowlio.me,https://www.flowlio.me — the bridge page, and nothing
# else. `*` is NEVER an acceptable value: this API answers to an administration token that lives on
# the user's machine. Set and empty is not the same as unset — an empty value means no web bridge
# at all, the API stops being reachable from a browser.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://flowlio.me,http://localhost:3000

# --- Production (Neon, Postgres 18) ---
# Never filled in this file, never committed. TLS mandatory: sslmode=require.
#
# DIRECT endpoint (migrations, `make up-prod`):
#   DATABASE_URL_PROD=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxx.REGION.aws.neon.tech/flowlio?sslmode=require
#
# POOLED endpoint (the API, host in «-pooler»): PgBouncer in transaction mode does not survive
# pgx's prepared-statement cache — add default_query_exec_mode=exec, or start-up is refused on
# purpose.
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/flowlio?sslmode=require&default_query_exec_mode=exec
